   "text": {
    "L1": "Natural materials come from plants, animals, or the earth and are used almost as they are.",
    "L2": "Wood, cotton, jute, wool, silk, stone, clay, and bamboo are natural materials.",
    "L3": "Human-made materials are made by people by changing natural materials a lot, usually in factories.",
    "L4": "Steel is human-made: people change iron ore using high heat and other factory processes.",
    "L5": "Here is a common myth: plastic is natural because it comes from crude oil.",
    "L6": "That is not true. People change crude oil a lot in factories, so plastic is human-made.",
    "L7": "Jute and cotton rot away in a few months, but plastic stays for hundreds of years and pollutes soil and water.",
    "L8": "Choose materials that suit the job, and reuse and recycle them. Now choose the human-made material."
   },
